  "summary": "The study compares four freestanding Ti3C2Tx-based films: pure MXene and electrostatically self-assembled M/G hybrids containing 1, 5, or 10 wt.% PDDA-modified rGO. Delaminated Ti3C2Tx was produced by LiF/9 M HCl etching of Ti3AlC2 followed by sonication; rGO served as an interlayer spacer. M/G-5% is the headline electrode, reaching 335.4 F g-1 and 1040 F cm-3 at 2 mV s-1 in 3 M H2SO4. Pure MXene had the highest stated volumetric capacitance, 1221.6 F cm-3 at 2 mV s-1, but markedly poorer rate retention. Film thickness, mass loading, areal capacitance, pore diameter, porosity, and numerical flake size were not reported."
}